**New evidence**
Wadas crackdown and project designation
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia: End harassment of residents opposed to 'national strategic project'","publisher":"Amnesty International Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-02-10","url":"https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/indonesia-end-harassment-of-residents-opposed-to-national-strategic-project/02/2022/","claim":"Amnesty said President Joko Widodo had designated the Bener Dam a national strategic project and that hundreds of security personnel entered Wadas, with residents reporting intimidation, arbitrary detention, and beatings.","locator":"opening paragraphs and background section","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights reporting with specific event details and direct mention of Jokowi's project designation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact February 2022 event in Jokowi's term.","ruler_attribution":"Direct for the national-strategic-project decision; indirect for the policing response through his administration.","contrary_evidence":["The deployment was framed by authorities as protecting land measurement for the project, not as punitive repression."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}
Wadas official findings
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Dugaan Kekerasan di Wadas, Komnas HAM Sampaikan Temuan Awal","publisher":"Komnas HAM","publication_date":"2022-02-14","url":"https://www.komnasham.go.id/index.php/news/2022/2/14/2079/dugaan-kekerasan-di-wadas-komnas-ham-sampaikan-temuan-awal.html","claim":"Komnas HAM said its early findings indicated violence by police during the land-measurement operation in Wadas and reported that some residents, including women and children, were traumatized and fearful of returning home.","locator":"summary paragraph and follow-up bullet on findings","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"National human-rights commission contemporaneous findings from its own monitoring and interviews.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate follow-up to the February 8, 2022 incident.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect; this concerns a provincial security operation under Jokowi's national executive, not a direct presidential order.","contrary_evidence":["Komnas HAM described this as preliminary findings, not a final legal adjudication of personal responsibility."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.4","3B.6","3B.8","3B.10"]}
Parigi Moutong shooting
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Usut dugaan penembakan pengunjuk rasa di Parigi Moutong, Sulawesi Tengah","publisher":"Amnesty International Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-02-13","url":"https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/usut-dugaan-penembakan-pengunjuk-rasa-di-parigi-moutong-sulawesi-tengah/02/2022/","claim":"Amnesty said a peaceful protester against a gold-mining operation in Parigi Moutong was shot and killed during police dispersal and urged the President to order an investigation and prosecution in civilian court.","locator":"background section and calls to action","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous advocacy reporting with specific casualty and response details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact February 2022 protest incident.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect for the police action; direct for the remedial authority Amnesty asked the President to exercise.","contrary_evidence":["The protest was not initially framed as a presidential order or national security action, and the shooting was still under investigation at publication."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.5","3B.9","3B.10"]}
Kanjuruhan response
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Soal Tragedi Kanjuruhan, Presiden: Usut Tuntas, Beri Sanksi yang Bersalah","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-10-03","url":"https://setkab.go.id/soal-tragedi-kanjuruhan-presiden-usut-tuntas-beri-sanksi-yang-bersalah/","claim":"Jokowi ordered a thorough investigation of the Kanjuruhan tragedy and said those proven guilty should be sanctioned; he also said he had instructed the relevant ministers and police leadership to handle the case.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted presidential remarks","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential secretariat transcript with date and explicit presidential instruction.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate response to the October 1, 2022 disaster.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Jokowi as president and head of the national executive.","contrary_evidence":["This is remedial action after the deaths, not prevention of the police misuse that triggered them."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.9","3B.10"]}
Kanjuruhan findings
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Police use of tear gas triggered Kanjuruhan stampede: Komnas HAM","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://en.antaranews.com/news/258265/police-use-of-tear-gas-triggered-kanjuruhan-stampede-komnas-ham","claim":"Komnas HAM said police firing tear gas was the main trigger for the Kanjuruhan stadium stampede, which killed 135 people.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the report on Komnas HAM's press conference","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting of Komnas HAM's formal findings with a precise causal claim and death toll.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 event and official aftermath.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect; the operational conduct was police action under Jokowi's administration rather than a personal presidential order.","contrary_evidence":["The direct trigger was police crowd-control practice, so this does not itself prove presidential direction."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.9","3B.10"]}
Kanjuruhan discipline
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"20 personel Polisi diduga langgar etik terkait tragedi Kanjuruhan","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.antaranews.com/berita/3165013/20-personel-polisi-diduga-langgar-etik-terkait-tragedi-kanjuruhan","claim":"Polri said 20 police personnel were suspected of ethical violations in connection with Kanjuruhan, and six officers were already designated as suspects in the broader investigation.","locator":"middle paragraphs describing the police statement and suspect list","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reporting of the police's own disciplinary and criminal-processing update.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Early October 2022 aftermath of Kanjuruhan.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect; this reflects institutional accountability within the national police under Jokowi's presidency.","contrary_evidence":["Internal discipline shows some remedy but does not establish complete accountability or adequate compensation."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.10"]}
Brigadir J response
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"On Police Murder Case, President Jokowi: Find the Truth","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/on-police-murder-case-president-jokowi-find-the-truth/","claim":"Jokowi ordered investigators to settle the Brigadir J case thoroughly, said nothing should be covered up, and urged them to find the truth.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted presidential remarks","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official transcript with explicit presidential instructions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 response to a major police-killing scandal.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Jokowi as president and overseer of the police hierarchy.","contrary_evidence":["This is post-incident accountability language rather than proof that abuse had been prevented earlier."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.9","3B.10"]}
Brigadir J accountability critique
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Kasus Brigadir J harus jadi momen penguatan akuntabilitas kepolisian","publisher":"Amnesty International Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-08-10","url":"https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/kasus-brigadir-j-harus-jadi-momen-penguatan-akuntabilitas-kepolisian/08/2022/","claim":"Amnesty said the Brigadir J case showed police accountability was still far from ideal and criticized a culture that protects fellow police and sustains impunity.","locator":"quoted remarks in the press release","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Advocacy statement, but it is specific about accountability deficits and tied to a concrete in-period case.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact August 2022 scandal and aftermath.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect to the police institution under Jokowi's executive authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is a normative accountability critique, not a judicial finding."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.4","3B.10"]}
Papua activists
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia: Free Imprisoned Papua Activists","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-08-15","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/08/15/indonesia-free-imprisoned-papua-activists","claim":"Human Rights Watch said Indonesian authorities continued to subject Indigenous Papuans to arbitrary arrests, torture, extrajudicial killings, and mass forced displacement, and urged release of activists prosecuted for peaceful expression and assembly.","locator":"first four paragraphs of the dispatch","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong rights-monitoring source summarizing a continuing pattern with specific allegations and contextual detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers the 2022 safety environment and continuing prosecutions.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: it describes the national security-force environment under Jokowi's presidency, especially in Papua.","contrary_evidence":["Some of the pattern predated 2022, so this is partly inherited baseline rather than fully ruler-created during the year."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.7","3B.8","3B.10"]}
Papua protest repression
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Papua krisis kebebasan berekspresi dan berkumpul","publisher":"Amnesty International Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-07-29","url":"https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/papua-krisis-kebebasan-berekspresi-dan-berkumpul/07/2022/","claim":"Amnesty said Indigenous Papuans protesting peacefully were met again with obstruction and excessive force by Indonesian police, including arrests of activists and blocking of demonstrations.","locator":"opening paragraph and quoted remarks from Usman Hamid","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local-language reporting on repeated police behavior during in-period protests.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact July 2022 protest cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect; the abuses were carried out by police in a region under national executive authority.","contrary_evidence":["This is advocacy reporting and does not by itself establish a presidential order to repress protest."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.3","3B.8","3B.10"]}
Papuan killings
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesian Soldiers Arrested for Killing 4 Papuans","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-09-02","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/09/02/indonesian-soldiers-arrested-killing-4-papuans","claim":"Authorities arrested six Indonesian soldiers suspected of killing and mutilating four Indigenous Papuans in West Papua, and HRW called for a broader inquiry into abuses.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong monitoring source with a concrete in-period case and named state actors.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact September 2022 incident.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect; the killings were by soldiers, but accountability runs through the national military chain under Jokowi's government.","contrary_evidence":["The arrests show some accountability, but the underlying abuse remains severe."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.4","3B.7","3B.10"]}
BBM protests
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Jokowi tanggapi rencana unjuk rasa tolak penyesuaian harga BBM","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-09-05","url":"https://www.antaranews.com/berita/3100121/jokowi-tanggapi-rencana-unjuk-rasa-tolak-penyesuaian-harga-bbm","claim":"Jokowi said Indonesia is a democracy and told protesters to express their aspirations well when reacting to planned protests over fuel-price increases.","locator":"first three quoted paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting of direct presidential remarks about protest handling.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Immediately before the September 2022 fuel protests.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Jokowi as the head of state responding to anticipated dissent.","contrary_evidence":["A permissive statement does not prove the police or local officials actually allowed protest without retaliation."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I considered roughly 30 documents across the presidential secretariat, Komnas HAM, Amnesty, HRW, Reuters/ANTARA syndication, and local reporting on Wadas, Parigi Moutong, Papua, Kanjuruhan, Brigadir J, and the BBM protests.
- I kept the sources that added distinct facts rather than repeating the same event through multiple publishers.
- I rejected later follow-ups from 2023-2026 unless they were only useful as context for the 2022 facts, because the chapter is scoped to 2022.
- I rejected general governance, economic, or constitutional articles that did not bear on physical safety, coercive institutions, protest protection, or accountability.
- I rejected duplicate mirrors and reprints when the same underlying claim was already available from an official transcript or a strong independent monitor.
- I also avoided re-fetching the structured datasets already present in the local prior; those remained the baseline rather than new evidence.

**Remaining gaps**
- The biggest gap is direct presidential chain-of-command evidence for the worst police and military abuses. The record shows Jokowi's public directives and post-incident accountability actions, but not detailed internal instructions before each incident.
- More evidence on implementation of remedies after Wadas, Parigi Moutong, Brigadir J, and Kanjuruhan would help determine whether the accountability response was durable or mostly symbolic.
- Papua remains the deepest unresolved safety area: the evidence clearly shows recurring abuses and arrests, but it is still mixed on how much of that pattern was actively driven, tolerated, or unsuccessfully constrained by Jokowi personally in 2022.
- Additional search could refine the attribution on police reform and oversight, but it is unlikely to overturn the central picture already established by the current record.
